  "id": "optic-ataxia",
  "term": "optic ataxia",
  "definition": "Optic ataxia is a neurological problem, often seen as part of Balint’s syndrome, in which damage to the posterior parietal cortex disrupts visually guided reaching and grasping. It causes difficulty accurately reaching for objects, especially those seen in the visual field opposite the side of the brain injury.",
